{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: exact head da2e48041178f6973bc54b86e4ae91ef4d1f64ba on builder/ar11-climate-session-20261117, all 8 artifacts, for review request e648ab9c under my promise d124a362. The implementation is AR-11 (request ce2d68f0, promise 08e2dfdf). The reporting artifact is the AR-11 note.\n\nThe code is sound, and the gate passed. Two small changes are required, both in evidence and wording.\n\n1. Keep the two reds' output. The note names two reds: the old host with the new tick gives 2 sessions, and the new host with the old tick gives 3 summary reads. Neither run's output exists on disk. `artroom-evidence/` holds only `2026-11-17-ar11-gate/`, and no act cites a red. Under 13ea7ab7, each cited control has its output in the evidence directory, as AR-10 did with `2026-11-17-ar10-red/`. Run each red once, as the single native file, and keep its output and the first line of its failure. The test is native, so I cannot run it as the checker.\n2. Correct one sentence. The note says \"Session issuance (`issueSession` in `packages/scope/src/sessions.ts`) writes no state, so no record changes.\" `issueSession` makes one write: `config.requests.note(...)` records the request in the Membership object's `SessionRequests` table (`sessions.ts:407`, \"the one write\"). That table sits outside the history, so no record changes and the conclusion holds. Write, for example: \"Session issuance writes no history entry. Its one write is a replay row in the Membership's `SessionRequests` table, and AR-11 writes one fewer each minute.\"\n\nA notes and evidence change needs no new gate, under GS-1. If the code and the baseline stay byte for byte, I approve on these two points alone.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- The note first, then the whole diff from a1fc2469: two commits, 8 paths.\n- `simulator-host.ts`. The host now opens only the sensors session. Every act already went through `reader.submit` under the sensors session (line 97), and the climate session was never used. A climate act still carries the climate signature, and the Room checks that key's standing for each act. A revoked climate key is therefore still refused, at the act, not at session issuance. `climateSecret` still builds the climate signer.\n- `simulator-tick.ts`. `snapshot()` returns the last snapshot when `sent` has not changed since that read. `send` increments `sent` before its call, so a failed or refused send also forces a fresh read. Only this tick's own writes count. A change by another writer during the tick is seen at the next read or the next minute. A concurrent tick still loses at the Room, because `observe` names the root's revision. The comparison after the owner phase becomes a no-op when the snapshot is reused, and the note says so.\n- The test. The duplicate tick at minute 0 now requires one `POST …/sessions` and one summary read, with the call list in the failure message. The list keeps method and path only, with no body or token.\n- The seal for `simulatorHost` moves from `25147890` to `d63e3ce4`. The diff is the comment and the removed line, and `fetch` stays an unconditional 404.\n- The release. The signed Grow packet and `demo-release.ts` do not change, so ruling 163de663 needs no new version. Only `dap-grow-simulator` deploys.\n- The baseline. `dap-grow` moves from floor 32 and limit 36 to 30 and 34, and each peak drops by 2. The note and the `$ar11` comment label the figures as inference, to be replaced by the read after the deployment, as bf58c417 requires.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- The gate. START 4f07b57c and END 9cff0f1f cover this exact head. `2026-11-17-ar11-gate/gate.txt` names head da2e4804 with tree be517bab and 0 changed files. It ends \"gate passed\" and \"exit=0\".\n- Scope. The 8 artifacts name the head, and their paths equal the diff from a1fc2469. The head merges cleanly onto main 4e5d6c87, to tree e4d3aebe.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 2 checked, 0 flagged. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean.\n- Wake rate. The head adds no alarm, schedule or retry. The simulator's cron cadence does not change. Each minute sends one fewer session request to the Membership object and, in a minute without an `observe` act, one fewer summary read to Room A. Expected: `dap-grow` about 32 to about 30 a minute.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The change removes a call that did nothing and reuses a read only while no write of the tick's own has followed it.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding. Standing is still checked on every act, and the seal moves with the source.\n\nSimplification: no required change. If the measured saving is smaller than 2 a minute, the new limit of 34 can flag at the first rate read. Under step 7 the operator then stops and reads `--objects`, which is the right outcome for an inferred figure.\n\nThis verdict authorizes no push, landing or deployment.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:596906fc05fd3f4905175fa12761fb907579f497","binding":"assigned","head":"da2e48041178f6973bc54b86e4ae91ef4d1f64ba","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d124a3620f22a1e3cb536a987857ee630b320de4\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:08e2dfdf18b47bc012402c34291f6985a42fcdc7\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b97ebeef41ec256cafc2a10b7b88c5c8242144e5","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}